A couple of weeks before the Dedham conference, Frank suggested that,
although I wasn't able to be physically at the conference, I should
consolidate various papers & mail messages together and e-mail the =
result
to Dedham (via the AMS) for input to the post-conference LaTeX workshop.
(I doubt whether he anticipated that the result would run to 138 pages!)

Frank now suggests that I should e-mail you all a copy.  I'll start to =
do
that tomorrow.

As far as I remember there's a root file, a .bbl file, and a number of
files that are \include-d.  In the hope of avoiding problems due to lack =
of
filestore at the receiving end, I'll mail a little every day for about 5
days.  I'll mail the root file last.  Thus, when you get the root file =
you
should have everything you need to typeset and print the document.

You'll have seen much of the material before, but may find it convenient =
to
have it all consolidated in one place.


David Rhead
JANET: d.rhead@uk.ac.nottingham.ccc.vme



